  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \nContinued the freeze warning across portions of central Ohio and the\nfrost advisory just west of the freeze warning. Temperatures will\ndrop off quickly this evening with light winds and mostly clear skies\nexpected. Temperatures will drop into the 30s across most locations\novernight. As the night progresses warmer air will start to move into\nthe area and winds will start to pick up. This will be more\nnoticeable across western portions of the region. Due to this there \nwill be less chance for frost across the west. Across the east there \nwill be a lack of moisture so frost is not expected to be widespread,\nbut do have patchy to areas of frost. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2) \nSeveral systems will bring showers and thunderstorms to the region.\nOne will move through Tuesday night into Wednesday. An active weather\npattern is expected over the weekend and into early next week with\nshower and thunderstorm chances each day. A System Monday afternoon\ninto Monday night is expected to be stronger and lead to more of a\npattern change.",
